              "text": "You’re missing the optimizer. Adam, the training algorithm, needs to store two extra copies of every parameter it updates: momentum and variance. In full fine-tuning, that’s three times the model size in memory. With LoRA, we only compute those states for the tiny LoRA matrices. The 175 billion frozen weights still sit in memory, but they don’t need optimizer states. That’s where the savings come from.",
